  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The full verb «sein» and denial",
   "texto": [
    "**Nicht** denies a full word or idea. Its position depends on what we want to deny; there is no general rule to put it always behind the verb. In these phrases it appears before the addition of origin: **Ich bin nicht aus Berlin** (not from Berlin), **Sie kommt nicht aus Deutschland** (not from Germany).",
    "Look at **sie**: with the verb in singular is «her.» (**sie ist**) and with the verb in plural is «They, they» (**sie sind**)."
